///     @ 0x00158 HDCP_CTRL            (P)
///               ###
///               * HDCP control register
///               ###
///               %unsigned 1  hdcp_version              0x0
///                                    ###
///                                    * This bit selects HDCP protocol version.
///                                    * 1: HDCP 2.X
///                                    * 0: HDCP 1.X
///                                    ###
///               %unsigned 1  hdcp22_clk_en             0x0
///                                    ###
///                                    * This bit is used to enable clock to 2.X HDCP HW engine.
///                                    * 1: 2.X HDCP HW engine's clock will be enable irrespective of hdcp_version bit.
///                                    * 0: 2.X HDCP HW engine's clock will be enabled only when hdcp_version bit is set.
///                                    ###
///               %unsigned 1  hdcp_avmute_en            0x0
///                                    ###
///                                    * 0: HDCP AVMUTE feature is disabled
///                                    * 1: HDCP AVMUTE feature is enabled
///                                    * HDCP AVMUTE feature is that, when it is in HDMI mode, if AVMUTE_set then frame counter shouldn’t increment, cipher state shouldn’t change.
///                                    * In the H/W HDCP engine this bit is anded with HDTX_GCP_CFG0[1] (avmute) bit.
///                                    ###
///               %unsigned 1  cipher_en                 0x0
///                                    ###
///                                    * 0: Cipher is disabled.
///                                    * 1: Cipher is enabled.
///                                    * Upon sensing hpd/rxsense, Ks register of block cipher gets initialized by PRBS data. In next pixel clock, the cipher gets enabled. It starts free run. Firmware resets this bit to zero at the end of free run period. Then in next 4 clock period An gets stored in tx_an register. This sets tx_an_ready to1.
///                                    ###
///               %unsigned 1  enh_link_verification     0x0
///                                    ###
///                                    * 0: Enhanced link verification is not set.
///                                    * 1: Enhanced link verification is set. In that case HDCP Tx & Rx may optionally support verification of cipher synchronization by comparing Pj (Pj’ from Rx) values for every 16th frame after authentication is over.
///                                    ###
///               %unsigned 1  advance_cipher            0x0
///                                    ###
///                                    * 0: advance_cipher disabled.
///                                    * 1: advance_cipher enabled.
///                                    * ADVANCE_CIPHER mode is an optional mode in which the cipher state and frame counter is advanced for every frame in DVI mode, or for every frame when not in AVMUTE state for HDMI mode, regardless of whether encryption is enabled or disabled. The HDCP Receiver indicates this capability by setting the 1.1_FEATURES Bcaps bit, and the HDCP Transmitters enables it by setting the ENABLE_1.1_FEATURES bit in the Ainfo byte.
///                                    ###
///               %unsigned 1  repeater                  0x0
///                                    ###
///                                    * 0: Rx is not a repeater.
///                                    * 1: Rx is a repeater.
///                                    ###
///               %unsigned 1  eess_en                   0x0
///                                    ###
///                                    * 0: OESS mode
///                                    * 1: EESS mode.
///                                    ###
///               %unsigned 1  aksv_sent                 0x0
///                                    ###
///                                    * If set, last byte of AKSV is transmitted to Rx. This triggers the authentication process to start. For every re-authentication this bit has to be cleared and set (0 -> 1).
///                                    ###
///               %unsigned 1  enc_en                    0x0
///                                    ###
///                                    * If set, indicates encryption is enabled for next frame and in progress until next encryption status signal comes. If enc_en=0 it indicates no encryption from the next frame. If for a particular frame enc_en is set then (if auth_done=2'b11) during win_of_opp just after Vsync edge, CTLX=1001 is sent. Else if enc_en is 0, then CTLX=0001 is sent
